# MORNING MOOD - Grieg, Peer Gynt Suite No. 1, Op. 46, no. 1 (written 1875, published 1888).
# The format is in Demo1/CLAUDE.md, under "Song files". Instruments are tables with
# one entry per frame; each channel holds named tracks; the lines at the end are the
# order list. In a track '.' holds and '-' releases. '#' starts a comment.
#
# Public domain: Grieg died in 1907. All 87 bars were read bar by bar off the
# full score in Brandon Amaro's 2022 edition (IMSLP 808246), dedicated to the public domain -
# the same edition as In the Hall of the Mountain King. The grace notes before the tune's
# second and third bars are left out: at a sixteenth a row there is no room for them.
# Grieg's slowing at the end is kept, as three steps of speed.
#
# The sunrise, as Grieg paints it. The flute plays the tune in E major; the oboe answers an
# octave down and turns it to G sharp; the flute takes it up in G sharp major; the oboe turns it
# again, through C sharp minor, to B; flute and oboe toss its last notes back and forth over a
# held B, louder each time - and at bar 21 the whole orchestra has the tune in E major, forte.
# It climbs to the sun at bar 30, G sharp major, fortissimo. The cellos sing under the violins'
# answers; the music slips to F major, and the cellos take the tune's head into D flat; it
# blazes out in D major at bar 46 and fades. A horn has the tune in F over rippling flutes, and
# a C augmented chord leads home: at bar 56 the cellos have it in E. Then it is quiet - a
# clarinet, birds in the flute, the horns swelling on B - and the flute plays the tune once
# more, as at the start, before the last chord. Then the song goes back to the beginning:
# morning, again.
#
# A row is a sixteenth, a line a bar of 6/8 at 60 dotted quarters a minute - Grieg's
# Allegretto pastorale.
#
# What four channels keep. Channel 1 is the bass, where the bassoons and cellos have it; channel
# 2 the held chords of the clarinets, horns and strings, one or two a bar. Both are on the
# pure-tone table in the octave below middle C, where it is within six cents of every note.
# Channels 3 and 4 are the tune on the 16-bit table: it climbs to F sharp 6, where the 8-bit
# table is thirty cents out. Soft in the flute, a reedier swell in the oboe, full in the strings.
#
# What is left out. Only one line of the orchestra can be the tune, so where Grieg has two -
# the violins' arpeggios over the cellos' song in bars 34-35 and 42-43 - the bar starts with
# the violins (an octave down) and ends with the cellos. The flutes' sixteenths under the horn
# in bars 50-53 are left to the chords, which the chip arpeggiates anyway. The horn, cello and
# bassoon tunes sound an octave up, clear of the chords. Chords are triads: the diminished
# seventh in bars 66 and 70 is C sharp minor over a G in the bass, and D flat augmented in bar
# 49 is a lone A over D flat.

song   MORNING MOOD
key    E MAJOR
rows   12
beat   6

instrument BASS
  table      tone
  volume     4 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 5 5 5 5 4
  distortion tone
  release    2

instrument BASS_F
  table      tone
  volume     10 11 11 10 10 9 9 9 8
  distortion tone
  release    2

# The held chords: a soft swell, arpeggiated as the chip plays every chord.
instrument PAD
  table      tone
  volume     2 3 4 4 5 5 5 5 5 4
  distortion tone
  release    1

instrument PAD_F
  table      tone
  volume     7 8 9 9 9 8 8 8 7
  distortion tone
  release    1

# The flute: breathed in, and a slow vibrato once the note has settled.
instrument FLUTE
  table      wide
  volume     6 8 9 10 10 9 9 9 8 8
  distortion tone
  vibrato    0 2 3 2 0 -2 -3 -2
  delay      14
  release    2

# The oboe: a quicker, reedier swell.
instrument OBOE
  table      wide
  volume     8 10 11 10 10 9 9 9 9 8
  distortion tone
  vibrato    0 2 3 2 0 -2 -3 -2
  delay      10
  release    2

# The strings in bar 21: the whole orchestra, forte.
instrument STRINGS
  table      wide
  volume     12 13 14 13 13 12 12 12 11
  distortion tone
  vibrato    0 3 4 3 0 -3 -4 -3
  delay      8
  release    2

# The strings, piano: dying away, or tranquillo.
instrument STRINGS_P
  table      wide
  volume     6 7 8 8 7 7 7 7 6
  distortion tone
  vibrato    0 2 3 2 0 -2 -3 -2
  delay      8
  release    2

# The cellos: warm and singing, a slow swell.
instrument CELLO
  table      wide
  volume     5 7 8 9 9 9 8 8 8 8
  distortion tone
  vibrato    0 2 3 2 0 -2 -3 -2
  delay      12
  release    3

# The horn: round, no vibrato.
instrument HORN
  table      wide
  volume     4 6 7 8 8 8 8 8 7
  distortion tone
  release    3

# The clarinet: plain and soft.
instrument CLARINET
  table      wide
  volume     6 7 8 8 8 7 7 7 7
  distortion tone
  release    2

